# naproxen.msf
# (S)-Naproxen  pKa=4.190 (COOH→COO-, q=0→-1)
# Source: Avdeef 2001 / NIST
# NSAID. Ionisation governs GI absorption and plasma protein binding.
# Carboxylate adjacent to a chiral centre with 2-naphthyl substituent.
# Clinical relevance: pKa below blood pH (7.4) → ~99.9% ionised in plasma.

